CHAPTER.VERS:
Flee, save your

          {+}
         lives, and be like a juniper in the wilderness.

How do you

          {+}
         say, We are mighty men, and valiant men for the war?

All you

          {+}
         who are round about him, bemoan him, and all you

          {+}
         who know his name; say, How is the strong staff broken, the beautiful rod!

Moab is put to shame; for it is broken down: wail and cry; tell

          {+}
         it by the Arnon, that Moab is laid waste.

Make

          {+}
         him drunk; for he magnified himself against Yahweh: and Moab will wallow in his vomit, and he also will be in derision.

O you

          {+}
         inhabitants of Moab, leave the cities, and stay in the rock; and be like the dove that makes her nest over the mouth of the abyss.
